title: The SPD in the Länder
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: spd_states = 1 and prussian_affairs_timer <= 0
on-arrival: prussian_affairs_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs
card-image: img/braun.jpg

= The SPD in the Länder

Our minister-presidents govern Lower Saxony, Brandenburg, Rhineland-Palatinate, Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, Hamburg, Bremen and the Saarland. In the Bundesrat, the Länder can block federal laws, and at home they run the police, the schools and the civil service.

What should our Länder governments do?

- @police_loyalty: Remove extremists from the state police.
- @police_strength: Hire more police officers.
- @bureaucracy: Pass a law to defend democracy in the civil service.
- @negotiate_concordat: Negotiate an end to the state payments to the churches.
- @sign_concordat: Sign the agreement with the churches.
- @root: No new policies are needed.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@police_loyalty
view-if: federal_police_loyalty < 1
on-arrival: federal_police_loyalty += 0.1

Chat groups with racist and far-right content have been found in police forces across the country. Our interior ministers set up independent police commissioners, vet recruits and dismiss officers who share extremist content.

Current police loyalty: [+ federal_police_loyalty : loyalty +].

@police_strength
on-arrival: federal_police_strength += 20

We hire more police officers in our Länder, especially in rural areas where people feel left alone by the state.

@bureaucracy
on-arrival: federal_police_loyalty += 0.05; democratization += 1; trust_in_democracy += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; afd_relation -= 3; firewall_erosion += 0.5

Applicants for the civil service are now checked against the files of the Verfassungsschutz, and members of groups rated as extremist can be dismissed. The AfD calls it a witch hunt against its members. Civil liberties groups are uneasy too.

@negotiate_concordat
view-if: prussian_concordat_progress < 1
on-arrival: prussian_concordat_progress += 1; cdu_relation += 2*(1-dissent);

The Basic Law has demanded an end to the state's historic payments to the churches since 1919, but no government has ever done it. Our Länder begin talks with the churches about a one-off settlement.

@sign_concordat
view-if: prussian_concordat_progress >= 1 and prussian_concordat = 0
on-arrival: prussian_concordat = 1; cdu_relation += 3; pensioners_spd += 1*(1-dissent); budget -= 1 if budget > 0

After a century, the Länder and the churches agree on a settlement. The churches receive a final payment over twenty years, and the yearly payments end. Both sides call it fair.
